---
# Root C-core style: the tree's own compact style (2-space, brace-attached,
# hand-shaped wraps), normalised to what machines and agents need:
#
# - ColumnLimit: 0 disables re-wrapping class-wide, so the tree's hand-shaped
#   signature wraps, packed struct typedefs and single-line macro bodies are
#   preserved as written. (With a column limit clang-format re-wraps them to
#   its own shapes; measured -w churn of the C core: 1491 lines with limit 100
#   vs 853 with limit 0 across the tree.)
# - AllowShort*: keeps the tree's unbraced single-line `if (x) y;` bodies.
# - SortIncludes: Never: include order in C is deliberate (internal headers
#   before system headers); never re-sorted.
# - AlignTrailingComments: false and the AlignConsecutive* LLVM defaults
#   (all off) keep edits local: realigning one line must not ripple into
#   neighbours.
#
# C++ frontends keep their own configs: frontends/fcitx5/.clang-format and
# frontends/tsf/.clang-format (4-space, same normalisation).
# Vendored and generated trees are excluded via .clang-format-ignore.
BasedOnStyle: LLVM
Language: Cpp
IndentWidth: 2
ColumnLimit: 0
AllowShortIfStatementsOnASingleLine: AllIfsAndElse
AllowShortLoopsOnASingleLine: true
AllowShortFunctionsOnASingleLine: All
AllowShortCaseLabelsOnASingleLine: true
AllowShortBlocksOnASingleLine: Always
AllowShortEnumsOnASingleLine: true
SortIncludes: Never
ReflowComments: false
AlignTrailingComments: false
DerivePointerAlignment: false
PointerAlignment: Right
